(4856816, 695418, 85097, '<td valign="top">at first glance this photo really pops.  After I look at it further, I cant put my finger on it.  It appears to be either over sharpened or maybe some type of filter effect applied to it.  It looks more "cartoonish" to me, and I am not sure if that was the effect you were going for?</td>', 'at first glance this photo really pops.  After I look at it further, I cant put my finger on it.  It appears to be either over sharpened or maybe some type of filter effect applied to it.  It looks more "cartoonish" to me, and I am not sure if that was the effect you were going for?', '2008-08-01 16:15:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(4856817, 699002, 73056, '<td valign="top">He''s beautiful!</td>', 'He''s beautiful!', '2008-08-01 16:15:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(4856818, 704233, 17513, '<td valign="top">my heart has just melted..simply beautiful.</td>', 'my heart has just melted..simply beautiful.', '2008-08-01 16:16:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(4856819, 704860, 85097, '<td valign="top">the image is a little too dark, which could work with a sunrise photo, but this could be tweaked to brighten the sky (make it a little more orange).  Also you are shooting directly into the sun, so it has created a lens flare.  Try using a lens hood, or not shooting directly into the sun to avoid the lens flare.</td>', 'the image is a little too dark, which could work with a sunrise photo, but this could be tweaked to brighten the sky (make it a little more orange).  Also you are shooting directly into the sun, so it has created a lens flare.  Try using a lens hood, or not shooting directly into the sun to avoid the lens flare.', '2008-08-01 16:16:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(4856822, 701042, 85097, '<td valign="top">I like the girl in the front left, the lighting is great on her face, but the girl in the back is a little out of focus and her eyes have no light in them.  Try using a reflector to bounce the light back into her face as well.</td>', 'I like the girl in the front left, the lighting is great on her face, but the girl in the back is a little out of focus and her eyes have no light in them.  Try using a reflector to bounce the light back into her face as well.', '2008-08-01 16:17:32.000000', NULL, 1),
