(4873563, 705403, 25678, '<td valign="top">the processing on this picture is dectracting rather than enhancing. I think there is too much sharpening going on... but I''m not sure</td>', 'the processing on this picture is dectracting rather than enhancing. I think there is too much sharpening going on... but I''m not sure', '2008-08-07 20:59:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(4873567, 705190, 17850, '<td valign="top">Amazing colors and of course very good angle!<br/>An amazing image! (10)</td>', 'Amazing colors and of course very good angle!An amazing image! (10)', '2008-08-07 21:00:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(4873568, 703721, 8860, '<td valign="top">I have a feeling that the weather got a little worse while in Photoshop! It''s a bit blue and heavy on the PP, so I just wonder if you''ve been compensating for some less than dramatic normality? If so, I would leave it more natural and emphasise detail and depth of darks rather than the colour. I''d do this in Lab colour mode and play with the levels in the Lightness channel which would give you a more natural result without blowing colours to the 4-winds. Otherwise, the composition is good.</td>', 'I have a feeling that the weather got a little worse while in Photoshop! It''s a bit blue and heavy on the PP, so I just wonder if you''ve been compensating for some less than dramatic normality? If so, I would leave it more natural and emphasise detail and depth of darks rather than the colour. I''d do this in Lab colour mode and play with the levels in the Lightness channel which would give you a more natural result without blowing colours to the 4-winds. Otherwise, the composition is good.', '2008-08-07 21:00:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(4873573, 703889, 8860, '<td valign="top">Lovely scene - good light. Just a tad oversharp.</td>', 'Lovely scene - good light. Just a tad oversharp.', '2008-08-07 21:02:42.000000', NULL, 1),
