(4876347, 703455, 82985, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=677021" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg"/></a>PostLuminous Award Nominee!<br/>sometimes, like here, the lack of DOF actually makes the image work, and gives the image a sense of depth and scale.  If the fence were also tack sharp, this would look flat and graphic.  As is, very deep and more dynamic.  The non-centered window and the angling upward fence, pointing at the focused subject really make this image work for me.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-08-08 22:37:14.</i></td>', 'PostLuminous Award Nominee!sometimes, like here, the lack of DOF actually makes the image work, and gives the image a sense of depth and scale.  If the fence were also tack sharp, this would look flat and graphic.  As is, very deep and more dynamic.  The non-centered window and the angling upward fence, pointing at the focused subject really make this image work for me.', '2008-08-08 23:35:57.000000', '2008-08-08 23:37:14.000000', 0),
