(4933299, 705385, 69008, '<td valign="top">Wow, by the comments, this is a "like it- don''t like it" kind of image, no middle ground. I''m in the like it pile.  Just a little more head on would have helped a lot with getting a better score I would think, but with animals we get only what they, the animals, will offer us.</td>', 'Wow, by the comments, this is a "like it- don''t like it" kind of image, no middle ground. I''m in the like it pile.  Just a little more head on would have helped a lot with getting a better score I would think, but with animals we get only what they, the animals, will offer us.', '2008-09-04 01:53:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4934648, 705263, 50695, '<td valign="top"><b>Zone Plate Photography</b> <br/> <br/><i>for Karen</i> <br/> <br/>I am eating Eggs Diavolo on the patio. Hungry bees<br/>are brushing the hotplate peonies. Ice cubes<br/>merely refract the excruciating intimacy of the sun.<br/> <br/>Glare is an old story: the violence of light. Tell me<br/>about the light that caresses, bending softly around<br/>an object in a delicate crescent, like a wave in a pool<br/> <br/>made by an insects leg. Give me only this gentle light<br/>upon my Charge-Coupled Device. Let my photoelectric sensors<br/>dotingly record each rise and fall, like an historian<br/> <br/>of dandelion spores, with compound eyes<br/>and wings of powdered paper, ecstatic for the touch<br/>that doesnt harrow me or hijack my flight.<br/></td>', 'Zone Plate Photography  for Karen  I am eating Eggs Diavolo on the patio. Hungry beesare brushing the hotplate peonies. Ice cubesmerely refract the excruciating intimacy of the sun. Glare is an old story: the violence of light. Tell meabout the light that caresses, bending softly aroundan object in a delicate crescent, like a wave in a pool made by an insects leg. Give me only this gentle lightupon my Charge-Coupled Device. Let my photoelectric sensorsdotingly record each rise and fall, like an historian of dandelion spores, with compound eyesand wings of powdered paper, ecstatic for the touchthat doesnt harrow me or hijack my flight.', '2008-09-04 17:23:33.000000', NULL, 0),
